---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Ceramics booking for schools and colleges"
	description="Wheel booking, kiln firing queues and class rosters for school and college ceramics departments with one or two kilns and a semester timetable."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">For schools and colleges</p>
			<h1>A ceramics department that runs on the timetable, not the whiteboard.</h1>
			<p class="lede narrow">
				One or two kilns, a semester of courses, and students booking wheels in the gaps between
				classes. Kilnbook keeps the wheels, the firing queue and the class rosters in one place.
			</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Wheel time between classes</h2>
		<p>
			Students reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks from their
			phone, so a free period turns into studio time instead of a queue. You set how many hours each
			group gets, how far ahead they can book, and what a no-show costs.
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">How wheel time works</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Firings that keep up with a semester</h2>
		<p>
			Students log each piece when they set it on the bisque shelf. Each kiln gets its own queue for
			bisque and glaze loads, with a firing log of the date, cone, schedule and who loaded it, and
			everyone with work in a load gets a text when it is ready for pickup.
			<a href="/features/firings">How firings work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Courses on the timetable</h2>
		<p>
			Set up each course as a fixed series, like Wheel 101 on Tuesdays for the semester. Instructors
			get their own login with the day's roster and can mark attendance from the studio tablet.
			Open sessions and waitlists work the same way for evening or community classes.
			<a href="/features/classes">How classes work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan fits a department?</h2>
		<p>
			The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns with unlimited members, wheel and table reservations, and
			class packs, waitlists and memberships, so a department with one or two kilns has room to
			grow. <a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
		<div class="faq">
			<details>
				<summary>Do schools get a discount?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Registered nonprofits and school ceramics programs get 30% off any plan. Mention it when
					you book a demo.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>We have two kilns. Which plan do we need?</summary>
				<p>
					The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns. If the department adds a fourth, you can move to
					Collective at any point in the month, and we prorate the difference on your next invoice.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Can we import our students from a spreadsheet?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Upload a CSV with names and emails, and we map the columns for you during setup.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Get your department off the sign-up sheet.</h2>
			<p>30 days free on the Studio plan. No card to start, and nothing is deleted if you walk away.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
